<title>PHILIPPINES: India, Malaysia offer rice to Philippines.</title>
<headline>India, Malaysia offer rice to Philippines.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysia and India had offered to supply up to 100,000 tonnes of rice each to the Philippines, a senior official of the Philippine Department of Agriculture told Reuters on Monday.  </p>
<p>&quot;We have received offers from the two countries for the supply of more rice,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>But another official at the state-owned National Food Authority (NFA) said the Philippines may not tap the Indian market for its rice procurement programme from neighbouring countries due to a &quot;bad experience&quot; in the past.</p>
<p>The official did not elaborate but traders said the supplies from India had not met quality standards.</p>
<p>NFA had imported rice from India in the past two years.</p>
</text>
